<Styles
    xmlns="https://github.com/avaloniaui"
    xmlns:x="http://schemas.microsoft.com/winfx/2006/xaml"
    xmlns:sys="clr-namespace:System;assembly=System.Runtime"
    xmlns:theme="clr-namespace:ApSolutions.LocalMedia.Presentation.Theme">
  <Styles.Resources>
    <ResourceDictionary>
      <!--
        The icon shapes ride in here rather than in App.axaml, and that is a measured choice: the
        four headless test applications load this file and nothing else of the theme, so an icon
        merged anywhere else would be missing from every suite that mounts a view — present in the
        product and absent from the gates, which is the worst of the two failures.
      -->
      <ResourceDictionary.MergedDictionaries>
        <ResourceInclude Source="avares://ApSolutions.LocalMedia.Presentation/Theme/Icons.axaml" />
      </ResourceDictionary.MergedDictionaries>
      <Thickness x:Key="FocusStrokeThickness">2</Thickness>
      <Thickness x:Key="FocusInnerStrokeThickness">1</Thickness>
      <x:Double x:Key="ControlHeight">36</x:Double>
      <!--
        The spacing scale, spent by all 186 spacing sites in src/ - Spacing, ItemSpacing, LineSpacing,
        RowSpacing and ColumnSpacing, which are all double and all say the same thing. Counted rather
        than chosen: 8 appeared 92 times, 12 forty-six, 4 twenty-one, 6 twelve, 16 six, 24 four, 2
        three times and 10 twice.

        12 is a step of its own and not a rounding. The gap from 8 to 16 is 2x and real use piles up
        inside it — 12 was the second most common value in the tree, a quarter of all its spacing — so
        mapping those forty-six sites to 8 or to 16 would move every one of them by a third, which is
        a visual decision taken by arithmetic rather than by design. The rest map to the nearest step
        and nothing in the application moves more than 2px: 6 to Space8, 2 to Space4, 10 to Space12.

        Numeric names and not XSmall/Small/Medium, because a semantic scale forces a new name to be
        invented every time a step turns out to be missing, and one just did: the alternative here
        was SpaceSmallMedium, which describes nothing. A number cannot lie about what it is.

        There is no Space32, for the same reason FontSizeMono is not declared: nothing spends it, and
        a scalar nobody reads is this repository's characteristic defect wearing a tidy name.
        ScalarTokenTests would refuse it. It arrives with the first site that asks for 32.

        Padding, Margin and BorderThickness keep their literals and are not on this scale. They are
        Thickness and these are x:Double, so the setter does not convert; and of the 89 literals
        those three properties carry, 37 are asymmetric - 0,8,0,0 and 48,0 and 8,4 - which no scalar
        token expresses at all.
      -->
      <x:Double x:Key="Space4">4</x:Double>
      <x:Double x:Key="Space8">8</x:Double>
      <x:Double x:Key="Space12">12</x:Double>
      <x:Double x:Key="Space16">16</x:Double>
      <x:Double x:Key="Space24">24</x:Double>
      <!--
        Two radii for the whole application, spent by all 37 CornerRadius sites in src/. Thirty of
        them were literals: 8 eighteen times, 4 five times, and 6, 10 and 12 seven times between them.

        Those seven looked like a missing step, because the 10s and the 12 are all card surfaces and a
        large card sharing a button's radius does look wrong. The tree said otherwise: of the seven
        surfaces painted with CardSurfaceBrush, four already carried 8. It was not a step being asked
        for, it was a split nobody decided, so all seven became Medium and the scale stays at two.
        The one site that moves more than 2px is the welcome card, and it moves into line with six
        others.

        These stay semantic where the spacing scale went numeric: two values with no gap between them
        cannot develop a missing step, which is the whole reason those had to be renamed.
      -->
      <CornerRadius x:Key="CornerRadiusSmall">4</CornerRadius>
      <CornerRadius x:Key="CornerRadiusMedium">8</CornerRadius>
      <!--
        The pill, and it is a third radius where the scale deliberately had two. What earns it is the
        rule the scale itself is held to: not "does the step make sense" but "does the tree contradict
        it". It does not - every button in the prototype is a pill, and §7 of the design proposal
        names the number rather than leaving it to be guessed: <b>CornerRadius=18, half the control
        height, not CSS's 999</b>. So it is one value spent by every button rather than a step for one
        consumer, which is the shape FontSizeMono was refused for.

        Half of ControlHeight, and the two are written apart because a CornerRadius is not a Double
        and AXAML has no arithmetic. ScalarTokenTests would not catch them disagreeing, so the comment
        is where the pair is declared: if the control height moves, this moves with it.
      -->
      <CornerRadius x:Key="CornerRadiusPill">18</CornerRadius>
      <!--
        The poster, in exactly 2:3, and here rather than inside PosterCardView because two things read
        it: the card paints it, and the library grid divides its own width by it to decide how many
        columns fit. Written in one place, the two cannot disagree — and they would, because the one
        that divides is C# and the one that paints is markup.

        148 is the width the prototype's library grid is approved at (minmax(148px, 1fr)); its rails
        use 132, and the wider of the two is the one a grid of them is measured against.
      -->
      <!--
        The one duration in the application, and the reason it is a TimeSpan token rather than a
        number: the animations read it and FluentThemeService WRITES it. When Windows asks for less
        motion the service puts TimeSpan.Zero here, so every animation goes to 0 ms - which is what
        reduced motion means, not a shorter animation.

        It used to be MotionDurationStandardMilliseconds, deleted with the scalars gate because
        nothing spent it and it was a parallel copy of a 160 living in the service. This is the same
        number arriving the way ReducedMotionTests said it should: declared once, read by the views,
        and the service reading from it instead of holding its own.
      -->
      <sys:TimeSpan x:Key="MotionDuration">00:00:00.160</sys:TimeSpan>
      <x:Double x:Key="PosterCardWidth">148</x:Double>
      <x:Double x:Key="PosterCardHeight">222</x:Double>
      <x:Double x:Key="TextControlPlaceholderOpacity">1</x:Double>
      <!--
        Five sizes for the whole application, mapped from the thirteen literals the views carried:
        34 and 32 to Display, 30/28/26 to Title, 24/22/20/18 to Subtitle, 17/16/14 to Body, 12 to
        Caption. FontSizeMono is still not declared: the three fixed-width surfaces read at body size
        and none of them asks for a size of its own, so it would be a scalar with one reader - which
        is what the scalars gate exists to refuse. The FAMILY is a different token and it is declared
        below, because three views spend it.
      -->
      <x:Double x:Key="FontSizeDisplay">32</x:Double>
      <x:Double x:Key="FontSizeTitle">28</x:Double>
      <x:Double x:Key="FontSizeSubtitle">20</x:Double>
      <x:Double x:Key="FontSizeBody">14</x:Double>
      <x:Double x:Key="FontSizeCaption">12</x:Double>

      <!--
        Fixed width, for the three surfaces where characters have to line up under each other: the
        diagnostics dump somebody reads before sharing it, the two paths of a rename, and the figures
        that tell one duplicate from another. Declared once now that three views spend it - one reader
        would have been the defect this repository names, which is why it lived as a literal until now.

        Three families and not one: Consolas ships with Windows, Cascadia Mono is what the terminal
        uses, and the generic name is what a host with neither falls back to.
      -->
      <FontFamily x:Key="FontFamilyMono">Consolas,Cascadia Mono,monospace</FontFamily>

      
      <!--
        The diagonal hatch over every poster, and it is the prototype's fourth layer — the one this
        application never drew. Its covers are four CSS backgrounds over one hue, listed top first:
        `repeating-linear-gradient(115deg, rgba(255,255,255,.055) 0 2px, transparent 2px 10px)`, a
        ring, a radial glow, and the two-stop gradient underneath. PosterArt built the glow and the
        base and stopped there, so the wall of colour was flat where the prototype's is woven — which
        is what the owner meant by the striped backgrounds being missing.

        Avalonia has no repeating gradient, and does not need one: a LinearGradientBrush with
        SpreadMethod="Repeat" tiles its own vector. The vector is ten pixels long at the CSS angle —
        115 degrees clockwise from north is (sin 115, -cos 115) = (0.906, 0.423) in screen
        coordinates, so (9.06, 4.23) — and the two hard stops at a fifth of it paint the first two of
        those ten pixels and leave the other eight alone. Absolute points rather than percentages,
        because a hatch that scaled with its card would be a different pattern on every tile.

        One brush for the four themes: the hatch is a fact about the artwork and not about the
        palette, exactly as it is in the prototype, and the two high contrast dictionaries switch the
        whole layer off through PosterArtOpacity rather than by having a hatch of their own.
      -->
      <LinearGradientBrush
          x:Key="PosterHatchBrush"
          SpreadMethod="Repeat"
          StartPoint="0,0"
          EndPoint="9.06,4.23">
        <GradientStop Offset="0" Color="#0EFFFFFF" />
        <GradientStop Offset="0.2" Color="#0EFFFFFF" />
        <GradientStop Offset="0.2" Color="#00FFFFFF" />
        <GradientStop Offset="1" Color="#00FFFFFF" />
      </LinearGradientBrush>

      <!--
        Four dictionaries, and every one of them carries the same twenty-three brushes. A brush missing
        from one theme falls back to whatever the base theme draws, which no contrast check covers,
        so ContrastTokenTests reads these dictionaries — the ones the application actually paints —
        rather than a parallel list of colours kept beside them. It used to read such a list: the
        colours said the control border was #475569 while the dictionary painted #64748B, and they
        described a HighContrastLight theme that no dictionary provided.
      -->
      <ResourceDictionary.ThemeDictionaries>
        <ResourceDictionary x:Key="Light">
          <SolidColorBrush x:Key="ShellSurfaceBrush" Color="#FBFCFE" />
          <!--
            The veil under the add-root dialog: the prototype's rgba(9,12,16,.62) over either
            ordinary theme, and opaque in the two high contrasts, where a half-seen page behind a
            dialog is clutter the theme exists to remove.
          -->
          <SolidColorBrush x:Key="ScrimBrush" Color="#9E090C10" />
          <!--
            The player's three, and they are the same in Light and Dark on purpose: what sits beside
            them is a picture, so the theme does not get a say. The chrome is the surface at 90 %,
            which is the prototype's own transport band, and the hairline is 10 % white - enough to
            separate the band from the frame above it without drawing a line across the film.

            In the two high contrast dictionaries both go solid. A band at 90 % over a moving picture
            has whatever contrast the frame behind it happens to give, and a 10 % hairline is not a
            line at all to somebody who needs the theme that asks for one.
          -->
          <SolidColorBrush x:Key="PlayerSurfaceBrush" Color="#0B0D10" />
          <SolidColorBrush x:Key="PlayerChromeBrush" Color="#E60B0D10" />
          <SolidColorBrush x:Key="PlayerPanelBrush" Color="#111820" />
          <SolidColorBrush x:Key="PlayerHairlineBrush" Color="#1AFFFFFF" />
          <!--
            The player's ink, and it exists because the player's surfaces are dark in all four modes
            while TextPrimaryBrush is dark in two of them. Measured on 2026-08-22: in Light,
            TextPrimaryBrush (#111827) on PlayerSurfaceBrush (#0B0D10) reads <b>1.10:1</b>, which is
            text nobody can see - the track pickers, the marker list and the versions panel all of
            them, on a machine whose Windows is set to light.

            The gate had a hole exactly that shape: it measured primary text on seven surfaces and
            the player's three were not among them. The eighth and ninth are measured now.
          -->
          <SolidColorBrush x:Key="PlayerTextBrush" Color="#F8FAFC" />
          <SolidColorBrush x:Key="PlayerTextSecondaryBrush" Color="#94A3B8" />
          <!--
            The poster's colour, on or off. The prototype paints every cover as a gradient built from
            the title's hue - four CSS gradients and not one image - and that is what makes a wall of
            covers look like a wall of covers. In the two high contrasts it goes to 0 and the card
            falls back to ControlFillBrush with its initials: an arbitrary hue behind two letters is a
            contrast ratio nobody chose, and somebody who asked the system for high contrast asked for
            the opposite of a decorative colour.
          -->
          <x:Double x:Key="PosterArtOpacity">1</x:Double>
          <!--
            The ink on a poster, and it lands on two different things. In Light and Dark it sits over
            the title's own gradient, whose darkest stop is 12 % lightness and whose lightest is 30 %,
            so near-white is legible over every hue the hash can pick - a ratio the token gate cannot
            measure, because the surface is computed rather than declared. In the two high contrasts
            PosterArtOpacity is 0, the gradient is not drawn, and the initials fall on
            ControlFillBrush - which is measured, one test below.
          -->
          <SolidColorBrush x:Key="PosterInitialsBrush" Color="#E6FFFFFF" />
          <SolidColorBrush x:Key="PosterChipInkBrush" Color="#EDF1F6" />
          <SolidColorBrush x:Key="PosterRingBrush" Color="#21FFFFFF" />
          <SolidColorBrush x:Key="NavigationSurfaceBrush" Color="#E9EEF4" />
          <SolidColorBrush x:Key="CardSurfaceBrush" Color="#FFFFFF" />
          <SolidColorBrush x:Key="ControlFillBrush" Color="#EDF1F6" />
          <SolidColorBrush x:Key="ControlFillHoverBrush" Color="#E3E9F1" />
          <SolidColorBrush x:Key="ControlFillPressedBrush" Color="#D8E0EA" />
          <SolidColorBrush x:Key="ControlFillDisabledBrush" Color="#F3F6FA" />
          <SolidColorBrush x:Key="ShellBorderBrush" Color="#6E7B8B" />
          <SolidColorBrush x:Key="ShellHairlineBrush" Color="#170F172A" />
          <SolidColorBrush x:Key="TextPrimaryBrush" Color="#101828" />
          <SolidColorBrush x:Key="TextSecondaryBrush" Color="#5A6675" />
          <SolidColorBrush x:Key="TextDisabledBrush" Color="#5F6B7A" />
          <SolidColorBrush x:Key="FocusStrokeBrush" Color="#005A9C" />
          <SolidColorBrush x:Key="FocusInnerStrokeBrush" Color="#FBFCFE" />
          <SolidColorBrush x:Key="AccentBrush" Color="#1769AA" />
          <SolidColorBrush x:Key="AccentSubtleBrush" Color="#E4EFF9" />
          <SolidColorBrush x:Key="AccentInkBrush" Color="#0B4A78" />
          <SolidColorBrush x:Key="ControlTextActiveBrush" Color="#101828" />
          <SolidColorBrush x:Key="AccentTextBrush" Color="#FFFFFF" />
          <SolidColorBrush x:Key="PrimaryActionBrush" Color="#1769AA" />
          <SolidColorBrush x:Key="PrimaryActionHoverBrush" Color="#15619D" />
          <SolidColorBrush x:Key="PrimaryActionPressedBrush" Color="#115586" />
          <SolidColorBrush x:Key="PrimaryActionTextBrush" Color="#FFFFFF" />
          <BoxShadows x:Key="ElevationShadow">0 1 2 0 #0D0F172A, 0 8 20 0 #0F0F172A</BoxShadows>
          <BoxShadows x:Key="ElevationShadowStrong">0 24 56 0 #330F172A</BoxShadows>
          <SolidColorBrush x:Key="WarningSurfaceBrush" Color="#FFF4E5" />
          <SolidColorBrush x:Key="WarningBorderBrush" Color="#7A4A00" />
          <SolidColorBrush x:Key="DangerSurfaceBrush" Color="#FDECEE" />
          <SolidColorBrush x:Key="DangerBorderBrush" Color="#8E1123" />
          <SolidColorBrush x:Key="PositiveSurfaceBrush" Color="#E6F4EA" />
          <SolidColorBrush x:Key="PositiveBorderBrush" Color="#0F5132" />
          <StaticResource x:Key="ButtonBackground" ResourceKey="ControlFillBrush" />
          <StaticResource x:Key="ButtonBackgroundPointerOver" ResourceKey="ControlFillHoverBrush" />
          <StaticResource x:Key="ButtonBackgroundPressed" ResourceKey="ControlFillPressedBrush" />
          <StaticResource x:Key="ButtonBackgroundDisabled" ResourceKey="ControlFillDisabledBrush" />
          <StaticResource x:Key="ButtonForeground" ResourceKey="TextPrimaryBrush" />
          <StaticResource x:Key="ButtonForegroundPointerOver" ResourceKey="ControlTextActiveBrush" />
          <StaticResource x:Key="ButtonForegroundPressed" ResourceKey="ControlTextActiveBrush" />
          <StaticResource x:Key="ButtonForegroundDisabled" ResourceKey="TextDisabledBrush" />
          <StaticResource x:Key="ButtonBorderBrush" ResourceKey="ShellBorderBrush" />
          <StaticResource x:Key="ButtonBorderBrushPointerOver" ResourceKey="ShellBorderBrush" />
          <StaticResource x:Key="ButtonBorderBrushPressed" ResourceKey="ShellBorderBrush" />
          <StaticResource x:Key="ButtonBorderBrushDisabled" ResourceKey="ShellBorderBrush" />
          <StaticResource x:Key="CheckBoxCheckBackgroundFillUnchecked" ResourceKey="ControlFillBrush" />
          <StaticResource x:Key="CheckBoxCheckBackgroundFillUncheckedPointerOver" ResourceKey="ControlFillHoverBrush" />
          <StaticResource x:Key="CheckBoxCheckBackgroundFillUncheckedPressed" ResourceKey="ControlFillPressedBrush" />
          <StaticResource x:Key="CheckBoxCheckBackgroundFillUncheckedDisabled" ResourceKey="ControlFillDisabledBrush" />
          <StaticResource x:Key="CheckBoxCheckBackgroundFillChecked" ResourceKey="AccentBrush" />
          <StaticResource x:Key="CheckBoxCheckBackgroundFillCheckedPointerOver" ResourceKey="ControlFillHoverBrush" />
          <StaticResource x:Key="CheckBoxCheckBackgroundFillCheckedPressed" ResourceKey="ControlFillPressedBrush" />
          <StaticResource x:Key="CheckBoxCheckBackgroundFillCheckedDisabled" ResourceKey="ControlFillDisabledBrush" />
          <StaticResource x:Key="CheckBoxCheckBackgroundStrokeUnchecked" ResourceKey="ShellBorderBrush" />
          <StaticResource x:Key="CheckBoxCheckBackgroundStrokeUncheckedPointerOver" ResourceKey="ShellBorderBrush" />
          <StaticResource x:Key="CheckBoxCheckBackgroundStrokeUncheckedPressed" ResourceKey="ShellBorderBrush" />
          <StaticResource x:Key="CheckBoxCheckBackgroundStrokeUncheckedDisabled" ResourceKey="ShellBorderBrush" />
          <StaticResource x:Key="CheckBoxCheckBackgroundStrokeCheckedPointerOver" ResourceKey="ShellBorderBrush" />
          <StaticResource x:Key="CheckBoxCheckBackgroundStrokeCheckedPressed" ResourceKey="ShellBorderBrush" />
          <StaticResource x:Key="CheckBoxCheckBackgroundStrokeCheckedDisabled" ResourceKey="ShellBorderBrush" />
          <StaticResource x:Key="CheckBoxCheckGlyphForegroundUnchecked" ResourceKey="AccentTextBrush" />
          <StaticResource x:Key="CheckBoxCheckGlyphForegroundUncheckedPointerOver" ResourceKey="ControlTextActiveBrush" />
          <StaticResource x:Key="CheckBoxCheckGlyphForegroundUncheckedPressed" ResourceKey="ControlTextActiveBrush" />
          <StaticResource x:Key="CheckBoxCheckGlyphForegroundUncheckedDisabled" ResourceKey="TextDisabledBrush" />
          <StaticResource x:Key="CheckBoxCheckGlyphForegroundChecked" ResourceKey="AccentTextBrush" />
          <StaticResource x:Key="CheckBoxCheckGlyphForegroundCheckedPointerOver" ResourceKey="ControlTextActiveBrush" />
          <StaticResource x:Key="CheckBoxCheckGlyphForegroundCheckedPressed" ResourceKey="ControlTextActiveBrush" />
          <StaticResource x:Key="CheckBoxCheckGlyphForegroundCheckedDisabled" ResourceKey="TextDisabledBrush" />
          <StaticResource x:Key="CheckBoxForegroundUnchecked" ResourceKey="TextPrimaryBrush" />
          <StaticResource x:Key="CheckBoxForegroundUncheckedPointerOver" ResourceKey="TextPrimaryBrush" />
          <StaticResource x:Key="CheckBoxForegroundUncheckedPressed" ResourceKey="TextPrimaryBrush" />
          <StaticResource x:Key="CheckBoxForegroundUncheckedDisabled" ResourceKey="TextDisabledBrush" />
          <StaticResource x:Key="CheckBoxForegroundChecked" ResourceKey="TextPrimaryBrush" />
          <StaticResource x:Key="CheckBoxForegroundCheckedPointerOver" ResourceKey="TextPrimaryBrush" />
          <StaticResource x:Key="CheckBoxForegroundCheckedPressed" ResourceKey="TextPrimaryBrush" />
          <StaticResource x:Key="CheckBoxForegroundCheckedDisabled" ResourceKey="TextDisabledBrush" />
          <StaticResource x:Key="SystemControlHighlightListLowBrush" ResourceKey="ControlFillHoverBrush" />
          <StaticResource x:Key="SystemControlHighlightListMediumBrush" ResourceKey="ControlFillPressedBrush" />
          <StaticResource x:Key="SystemControlHighlightListAccentLowBrush" ResourceKey="AccentSubtleBrush" />
          <!--
            The drop-down, in three families of its own: the closed frame, the panel that opens, and
            the rows inside it. Measured: 59 keys, and it inherits nothing from the text field
            because IsEditable appears nowhere in the tree.
          -->
          <StaticResource x:Key="ComboBoxBackground" ResourceKey="ControlFillBrush" />
          <StaticResource x:Key="ComboBoxBackgroundPointerOver" ResourceKey="ControlFillHoverBrush" />
          <StaticResource x:Key="ComboBoxBackgroundPressed" ResourceKey="ControlFillPressedBrush" />
          <StaticResource x:Key="ComboBoxBackgroundDisabled" ResourceKey="ControlFillDisabledBrush" />
          <StaticResource x:Key="ComboBoxBackgroundUnfocused" ResourceKey="AccentSubtleBrush" />
          <StaticResource x:Key="ComboBoxBackgroundBorderBrushUnfocused" ResourceKey="ShellBorderBrush" />
          <StaticResource x:Key="ComboBoxBorderBrush" ResourceKey="ShellBorderBrush" />
          <StaticResource x:Key="ComboBoxBorderBrushPointerOver" ResourceKey="ShellBorderBrush" />
          <StaticResource x:Key="ComboBoxBorderBrushPressed" ResourceKey="ShellBorderBrush" />
          <StaticResource x:Key="ComboBoxBorderBrushDisabled" ResourceKey="ShellBorderBrush" />
          <StaticResource x:Key="ComboBoxForeground" ResourceKey="TextPrimaryBrush" />
          <StaticResource x:Key="ComboBoxForegroundFocused" ResourceKey="TextPrimaryBrush" />
          <StaticResource x:Key="ComboBoxForegroundFocusedPressed" ResourceKey="ControlTextActiveBrush" />
          <StaticResource x:Key="ComboBoxForegroundDisabled" ResourceKey="TextDisabledBrush" />
          <StaticResource x:Key="ComboBoxDropDownGlyphForeground" ResourceKey="TextPrimaryBrush" />
          <StaticResource x:Key="ComboBoxDropDownGlyphForegroundFocused" ResourceKey="TextPrimaryBrush" />
          <StaticResource x:Key="ComboBoxDropDownGlyphForegroundFocusedPressed" ResourceKey="TextPrimaryBrush" />
          <StaticResource x:Key="ComboBoxDropDownGlyphForegroundDisabled" ResourceKey="TextDisabledBrush" />
          <StaticResource x:Key="ComboBoxPlaceHolderForeground" ResourceKey="TextSecondaryBrush" />
          <StaticResource x:Key="ComboBoxPlaceHolderForegroundFocusedPressed" ResourceKey="TextSecondaryBrush" />
          <StaticResource x:Key="ComboBoxDropDownBackground" ResourceKey="CardSurfaceBrush" />
          <StaticResource x:Key="ComboBoxDropDownBorderBrush" ResourceKey="ShellBorderBrush" />
          <StaticResource x:Key="ComboBoxItemBackgroundPointerOver" ResourceKey="ControlFillHoverBrush" />
          <StaticResource x:Key="ComboBoxItemBackgroundPressed" ResourceKey="ControlFillPressedBrush" />
          <StaticResource x:Key="ComboBoxItemBackgroundSelected" ResourceKey="AccentSubtleBrush" />
          <StaticResource x:Key="ComboBoxItemBackgroundSelectedPointerOver" ResourceKey="ControlFillHoverBrush" />
          <StaticResource x:Key="ComboBoxItemBackgroundSelectedPressed" ResourceKey="ControlFillPressedBrush" />
          <StaticResource x:Key="ComboBoxItemForeground" ResourceKey="TextPrimaryBrush" />
          <StaticResource x:Key="ComboBoxItemForegroundPointerOver" ResourceKey="ControlTextActiveBrush" />
          <StaticResource x:Key="ComboBoxItemForegroundPressed" ResourceKey="ControlTextActiveBrush" />
          <StaticResource x:Key="ComboBoxItemForegroundSelected" ResourceKey="TextPrimaryBrush" />
          <StaticResource x:Key="ComboBoxItemForegroundSelectedPointerOver" ResourceKey="ControlTextActiveBrush" />
          <StaticResource x:Key="ComboBoxItemForegroundSelectedPressed" ResourceKey="ControlTextActiveBrush" />
          <StaticResource x:Key="ComboBoxItemForegroundDisabled" ResourceKey="TextDisabledBrush" />
          <StaticResource x:Key="ComboBoxItemForegroundSelectedDisabled" ResourceKey="TextDisabledBrush" />
          <!--
            Phase 2g: the slider, the toggle and the radio. Eight uses between them and one grammar
            of states, so they are aliases and not a fourth way of saying the same thing. Two
            families are left alone on purpose, because nothing in the tree can reach them: the
            toggle's Indeterminate* (IsThreeState appears nowhere) and the slider's tick bar (no
            view sets TickPlacement, so no tick is drawn).
          -->
          <StaticResource x:Key="SliderTrackValueFill" ResourceKey="AccentBrush" />
          <StaticResource x:Key="SliderTrackValueFillPointerOver" ResourceKey="AccentBrush" />
          <StaticResource x:Key="SliderTrackValueFillPressed" ResourceKey="AccentBrush" />
          <StaticResource x:Key="SliderTrackValueFillDisabled" ResourceKey="TextSecondaryBrush" />
          <StaticResource x:Key="SliderTrackFill" ResourceKey="ControlFillBrush" />
          <StaticResource x:Key="SliderTrackFillPointerOver" ResourceKey="ControlFillHoverBrush" />
          <StaticResource x:Key="SliderTrackFillPressed" ResourceKey="ControlFillPressedBrush" />
          <StaticResource x:Key="SliderTrackFillDisabled" ResourceKey="ControlFillDisabledBrush" />
          <StaticResource x:Key="SliderThumbBackground" ResourceKey="AccentBrush" />
          <StaticResource x:Key="SliderThumbBackgroundPointerOver" ResourceKey="AccentBrush" />
          <StaticResource x:Key="SliderThumbBackgroundPressed" ResourceKey="AccentBrush" />
          <StaticResource x:Key="SliderThumbBackgroundDisabled" ResourceKey="ControlFillDisabledBrush" />
          <StaticResource x:Key="ToggleButtonBackground" ResourceKey="ControlFillBrush" />
          <StaticResource x:Key="ToggleButtonBackgroundPointerOver" ResourceKey="ControlFillHoverBrush" />
          <StaticResource x:Key="ToggleButtonBackgroundPressed" ResourceKey="ControlFillPressedBrush" />
          <StaticResource x:Key="ToggleButtonBackgroundDisabled" ResourceKey="ControlFillDisabledBrush" />
          <StaticResource x:Key="ToggleButtonBackgroundChecked" ResourceKey="AccentBrush" />
          <StaticResource x:Key="ToggleButtonBackgroundCheckedPointerOver" ResourceKey="ControlFillHoverBrush" />
          <StaticResource x:Key="ToggleButtonBackgroundCheckedPressed" ResourceKey="ControlFillPressedBrush" />
          <StaticResource x:Key="ToggleButtonBackgroundCheckedDisabled" ResourceKey="ControlFillDisabledBrush" />
          <StaticResource x:Key="ToggleButtonBorderBrush" ResourceKey="ShellBorderBrush" />
          <StaticResource x:Key="ToggleButtonBorderBrushPointerOver" ResourceKey="ShellBorderBrush" />
          <StaticResource x:Key="ToggleButtonBorderBrushPressed" ResourceKey="ShellBorderBrush" />
          <StaticResource x:Key="ToggleButtonBorderBrushDisabled" ResourceKey="ShellBorderBrush" />
          <StaticResource x:Key="ToggleButtonBorderBrushChecked" ResourceKey="ShellBorderBrush" />
          <StaticResource x:Key="ToggleButtonBorderBrushCheckedPointerOver" ResourceKey="ShellBorderBrush" />
          <StaticResource x:Key="ToggleButtonBorderBrushCheckedPressed" ResourceKey="ShellBorderBrush" />
          <StaticResource x:Key="ToggleButtonBorderBrushCheckedDisabled" ResourceKey="ShellBorderBrush" />
          <StaticResource x:Key="ToggleButtonForeground" ResourceKey="TextPrimaryBrush" />
          <StaticResource x:Key="ToggleButtonForegroundPointerOver" ResourceKey="ControlTextActiveBrush" />
          <StaticResource x:Key="ToggleButtonForegroundPressed" ResourceKey="ControlTextActiveBrush" />
          <StaticResource x:Key="ToggleButtonForegroundDisabled" ResourceKey="TextDisabledBrush" />
          <StaticResource x:Key="ToggleButtonForegroundChecked" ResourceKey="AccentTextBrush" />
          <StaticResource x:Key="ToggleButtonForegroundCheckedPointerOver" ResourceKey="ControlTextActiveBrush" />
          <StaticResource x:Key="ToggleButtonForegroundCheckedPressed" ResourceKey="ControlTextActiveBrush" />
          <StaticResource x:Key="ToggleButtonForegroundCheckedDisabled" ResourceKey="TextDisabledBrush" />
          <StaticResource x:Key="RadioButtonOuterEllipseStroke" ResourceKey="ShellBorderBrush" />
          <StaticResource x:Key="RadioButtonOuterEllipseStrokePointerOver" ResourceKey="ShellBorderBrush" />
          <StaticResource x:Key="RadioButtonOuterEllipseStrokePressed" ResourceKey="ShellBorderBrush" />
          <StaticResource x:Key="RadioButtonOuterEllipseStrokeDisabled" ResourceKey="ShellBorderBrush" />
          <StaticResource x:Key="RadioButtonOuterEllipseFill" ResourceKey="ControlFillBrush" />
          <StaticResource x:Key="RadioButtonOuterEllipseFillPointerOver" ResourceKey="ControlFillHoverBrush" />
          <StaticResource x:Key="RadioButtonOuterEllipseFillPressed" ResourceKey="ControlFillPressedBrush" />
          <StaticResource x:Key="RadioButtonOuterEllipseFillDisabled" ResourceKey="ControlFillDisabledBrush" />
          <StaticResource x:Key="RadioButtonOuterEllipseCheckedFill" ResourceKey="AccentBrush" />
          <StaticResource x:Key="RadioButtonOuterEllipseCheckedFillPointerOver" ResourceKey="ControlFillHoverBrush" />
          <StaticResource x:Key="RadioButtonOuterEllipseCheckedFillPressed" ResourceKey="ControlFillPressedBrush" />
